SUMMARY:Wednesday night Bent Creek
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nHard Times Trailhead near Lake Pow
 hatan Rec Area\nWeather: T-Storms are predicted\, I'll let you know if it'
 s raining\, and/or cancelled.\nI did this hike series for many years befor
 e 2022\, but I did it as a high-speed hike\, and I am now doing it as a mo
 derate speed hike. This is a numbers limited event and I expect people who
  sign-up to show up. Late cancellations\, and those that don't show up are
  bumping other interested hikers\, and they will not be allowed on future 
 hikes.\nIf all goes well\, I will try to post a hike most weeks\, and for 
 days Tue or Wed\, distance\, and start location\, like switching between H
 ard Times trail-head and Bent Creek River Park\, may change.\nThe current 
 route is about 5.5 miles.\nPlease folks\, this is intended as a moderate p
 aced hike\, and we'd like all attendees to keep up with the hike leader(s)
 . This hike is intended as a workout hike for people to get in condition t
 o do weekend hikes.\nModerate paced means 22-24 min miles\, or 2 ½ mph.\n
 As such\, we do not take breaks\, take in views\, or snap photos along the
  way. Please make sure you're able to keep up with the group. This hike ha
 s always served as a good chance to get exercise during the week\, meet ne
 w people\, and create interest for weekend enjoyment hikes. It's a great i
 ntroduction to the AHG family.\nNo need to RSVP "No" or "not attending" un
 less changing from a "Yes."\nPlease read the full description before RSVPi
 ng\, and only sign up if you are sure you can go. Thanks in advance for ke
 eping your RSVP up-to-date and not being a last-minute cancellation or no-
 show. This is an ongoing issue with Meetups and often keeps people on wait
 lists from being able to attend our hikes.\nHard Times Trailhead near Lake
  Powhatan Rec Area\nFollow signs off of Brevard Rd (Rt 191) to Lake Powhat
 an Rec Area. The road is Bent Creek Ranch Rd. to Wesley Branch Rd. Follow 
 signs to Lake Powhatan until you come to Hard Times Trailhead on your left
 \, 2.5 miles. It is very clearly marked. Parking is very limited at the tr
 ailhead but there’s a paved pull-off just before the Hard Times trailhea
 d and more parking just beyond at the Ledford Branch trailhead. We will ac
 cess Bent Creek forest by way of Hard Times Trail and do some combination 
 of loop and out and back.\nArrive at the trailhead BY 6:00. Because it is 
 a weeknight hike\, we are unable to wait for latecomers\, fighting dayligh
 t.\n\\*\\*\\*If you are running behind\, please post a comment on this Mee
 tup page by 5:45 pm. There is no cell service at the parking lot\, so if w
 e don't have any advance notice of you running late by 5:45\, we can't get
  any notifications at the trailhead and we will not wait for you.\nWe star
 t the hike at 6:00\, rarely do we get much later than that.\n• Wear clos
 ed-toed footwear appropriate for hiking. The trail will consist of dirt\, 
 rocks\, roots\, mud and mulch.\n• Bring plenty of water.\n• Bring rain
  gear if a chance of rain is in the forecast.\nHeadlamps suggested\n• Do
 gs on leashes the whole time are welcome. This is an active mountain bike 
 area and it can get messy with dogs running loose among hikers and mountai
 n bikers.\nPlease make sure to keep your RSVP up-to-date. You don't want t
 o be "that person" who cancels last minute or no-shows and keeps someone f
 rom joining in if there's a waitlist. Thanks for your consideration - it i
 s appreciated!\nFeel free to post questions not covered in this descriptio
 n in the comments section.\nThanks - we'll see you on the trail!\nDisclaim
 er and Release of Liability:\nThis activity involves hiking on city street
 s that may have traffic and/or natural trails with roots\, rocks\, and ste
 ep sections. Participants are responsible for their safety on streets and 
 trails. The organizer of this trip is a volunteer and not a professional g
 uide. The function of the organizer is only to organize this trip. If you 
 sign up or participate in this event you acknowledge that you freely and v
 oluntarily agree to assume all risks of injuries\, illnesses\, and damages
  arising from\, as a result of\, and associated with this event. In additi
 on\, you acknowledge that you agree to the Meetup terms: [https://www.meet
 up.com/terms](https://www.meetup.com/terms)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/315445829
 /
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260627T202553Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260627T202553Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
