X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_ashevillehikinggroup
X-SOURCE:Asheville Hiking Group
UID:event_315445049@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260628T043140Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260703T084500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260703T123000
SUMMARY:Looking Glass Rock - 6 Mi\, 1700 Ft EG
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**DETAILS**\n\n* 6 Miles\, 1700 Fe
 et Elevation Gain so a Moderate level\n* Carpool - 8am at Tanger Outlets p
 arking lot behind the Waffle House (link labeled Asheville Outlets)\, 8:35
  at Pisgah Ranger Station Outer Loop\n* Hike Start - 8:45 at Trailhead htt
 ps://maps.app.goo.gl/3zsHykkoJwRB23neA\n* Sign up starts at 8pm Sunday\, I
  am keeping group small this week.\n\nThis is a busy trail but one that I 
 don't do often enough. The hike departs from the trailhead on Fish Hatcher
 y Road and begins winding its way along switchbacks to the top. This is a 
 gradual ascent. A couple of miles into our hike\, we will come across a fl
 at\, rocky area that is used as a helicopter landing zone for rock climber
 s and hikers needing rescue. We will walk off the main trail here for an a
 mazing view! Next we will stop at the top on the rock for a snack and time
  to absorb the views before heading back down.\n\n**CARPOOL**\nParking can
  be tough so we will start early this week. I want to start hiking by 8:45
  so that means we need to leave the Tanger Outlets by 8am. We will stop by
  the Pisgah Ranger Station at 8:35 and pick up all folks meeting there. Pl
 ease be a little early to each of the carpool stops.\n\n**WEATHER**\nI'll 
 watch the weather and post a cancellation message by 7:00 AM if the foreca
 st is >50% chance of precipitation.\n\n**QUESTIONS?**\nYou can message me 
 through MeetUp until 8:00 AM the day of. Cell reception may be sketchy\, b
 ut you can try to text or call me up to the start of the hike: (508) 965-2
 333.\n\n**LEGALESE**\nThis Asheville Hiking Group event involves hiking an
 d\, possibly\, transportation to and from the meetup site. Participants ar
 e responsible for their own safety and affirm that they have the appropria
 te skills\, physical conditioning\, equipment\, and supplies. Hiking may i
 nvolve risks to oneself and property. Neither your hike organizer nor Ashe
 ville Hiking Group can assure your safety nor eliminate all risks. Partici
 pants assume full responsibility for any injuries\, damages\, or losses.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/315445049
 /
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260627T190759Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260627T190759Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Haywood County Walking Meetup Group": "https://www.meetup.com/haywood-county-walking-meetup-group/events/314585809/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_haywood_county_walking_meetup_group
X-SOURCE:Haywood County Walking Group
UID:event_314585809@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260628T043148Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260703T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260703T123000
SUMMARY:Historic Columbia SC Morning Walk—Governor's Mansion\, Finlay Pa
 rk\, and More!
DESCRIPTION:Haywood County Walking Meetup Group\nMeet at 10:00 a.m. in the
  lobby of the Hampton Inn\, 822 Gervais Street\, Columbia 29223 (enter the
  lobby from the Lincoln Street side). Restrooms are available at the start
  point.\n\nThe trail takes you past the Woodrow Wilson Boyhood Home\, arou
 nd the Governor's Mansion\, through the newly reopened Finlay Park\, and t
 hrough Memorial Park.\n\nThere are some moderate hills and stair climbing\
 , but it is almost entirely on pavement. Tennis shoes are fine\; some may 
 want walking sticks or hiking boots.\n\nDress for the weather. It will lik
 ely be very hot. A hat and sunscreen are highly recommended.\n\n**Plenty o
 f water** and a protein snack are advised as always. Wheelchairs are not r
 ecommended\, although strollers ought to be ok. Dogs are welcome.\n\nOur M
 eetup group offers some version of this walk every three months. It's that
  good! You will surely enjoy it.\n\nTraditionally\, many of us eat at Five
  Guys (near the start point) after the walk. There are lots of other resta
 urants nearby. Give yourself plenty of time to enjoy your meal after you j
 oin the group for the walk.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/haywood-county-walking-meetup-group/e
 vents/314585809/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260501T224119Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260501T224119Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
