LAST-MODIFIED:20260527T182127Z
UID:10006705-1784505600-1784591999@www.ashevilleart.org
SUMMARY:Summer Art Camp | Fun with Fiber Art (Rising K - 2nd grade)
DESCRIPTION:JOIN THE WAITLIST \nLearn to weave\, felt with wool\, collage with paper and much more during this week focusing on fiber art! Students will explore different materials and methods of creating artworks with yarn\, thread\, fabric\, and more!  \nMeet the Instructor: M Rathsack\nM Rathsack\, owner and instructor at M’s School of Art\, has taught many mediums in many locations for all ages in Western North Carolina since 2006. She creates her own art as the Dancing Potter working primarily as a decorative raku potter. 
URL:https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/summer-art-camp-fun-with-fiber-art-rising-k-2nd-grade-3/
LOCATION:NC
CATEGORIES:Summer Art Camp
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ashevilleart.org/wp-content/uploads/2014.37.34_verso-scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ashevilleart": "https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/summer-art-camp-art-our-environment-rising-k-2nd-grade-2/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ashevilleart
X-SOURCE:Asheville Art Museum
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260720
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260721
DTSTAMP:20260527T182352Z
CREATED:20260527T182352Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260527T182352Z
UID:10006661-1784505600-1784591999@www.ashevilleart.org
SUMMARY:Summer Art Camp | Art & Our Environment (Rising K - 2nd grade)
DESCRIPTION:JOIN THE WAITLIST \nStudents will explore art and the environment through a series of mixed-media projects. Students will create collages of animal habitats using recycled materials and mountain landscapes featuring local wildlife. Students will be encouraged to use personal expression\, gain environmental awareness\, and learn creative problem-solving. Students will conclude the week by creating mixed-media memory boxes or shadow boxes filled with hand-built clay creatures.  \nMeet the Instructor: Julia Worden\nJulia Worden holds a master’s degree in art education and teaches visual art in Western North Carolina. She is passionate about working with learners of all ages and is dedicated to fostering confidence\, critical thinking\, and the development of individual artistic voices. Having spent seven years living abroad\, Julia engaged extensively with galleries\, artistic events\, and diverse art communities across Europe\, experiences she now weaves into her teaching to deepen students’ understanding and connection to art. Outside the studio and classroom\, she enjoys reading\, baking\, and spending time with her cats\, Cas and Nyx. 
URL:https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/summer-art-camp-art-our-environment-rising-k-2nd-grade-2/
LOCATION:NC
CATEGORIES:Summer Art Camp
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ashevilleart.org/wp-content/uploads/2021.76.04_alt1.jpg
END:VEVENT
